Contribution to the World Organistion for Animal health (OIE) to support ODA eligible countries with antimicrobial resistance (AMR) National Action Plans, the development of global protocols for collection of AMR and antimicrobial use and consumption data, and in-country activities to tackle AMR. 
The objectives of the Fleming Fund grant with OIE are to: 
1. To support the development and implementation of national action plans on AMR that are aligned by the global action plan and with intergovernmental standards and guidelines established by Codex Alimentarius and the OIE; 
2. To support coordinated surveillance and reporting on AMR in human and animal health and agriculture in LMICs; 
3. To collect, consolidate and publish information on the global consumption of antimicrobial medicines for each sector (human and animal health); 
4. To strengthen and review the concepts of critically important antibiotics for human and animal health; 
5.To develop standards and guidance, based on the best available evidence; and 
6.To improve awareness and understanding of AMR through effective communication, education and training.

